\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qc\kerning2\ul\b\f0\fs40\lang16393 LangChain: Connecting RAG Components\par
\fs24\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\ulnone\b0 LangChain is an open-source framework that helps developers build applications powered by Large Language Models (LLMs) such as GPT, Gemini, Claude, and Llama.\par
Its main purpose is to connect different AI components together so that an LLM can work with external data, tools, APIs, and databases.\par
\par
A standalone LLM only knows what it learned during training. LangChain helps the LLM:\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Read documents (PDFs, Word files, websites)\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Store and search knowledge using vector databases\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Retrieve relevant information (RAG)\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Use external APIs and tools\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Maintain conversation memory\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Build AI agents that can perform tasks\par

\pard\widctlpar\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\par
\fs40  Pipeline:\par
\fs24\par

\pard\widctlpar\li360\sa160\sl276\slmult1\b Document Loading\b0\par
Load data from PDFs, Word files, websites, databases, etc.\par
Example: PyPDFLoader, TextLoader, WebBaseLoader.\par
\b Document Splitting\b0\par
Break large documents into smaller chunks.\par
Improves retrieval accuracy and reduces token usage.\par
Example: RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter.\par
\b Embedding\b0\par
Convert text chunks into numerical vectors.\par
Similar meanings produce similar vectors.\par
Example models: \par

\pard\widctlpar\li1080\sa160\sl276\slmult1 OpenAI Embeddings\par
Hugging Face Embeddings\par
Sentence Transformers\par

\pard\widctlpar\li360\sa160\sl276\slmult1\b Vector Store\b0\par
Store embeddings in a vector database.\par
Examples: \par

\pard\widctlpar\li1080\sa160\sl276\slmult1 FAISS\par
ChromaDB\par
Pinecone\par
Weaviate\par

\pard\widctlpar\li360\sa160\sl276\slmult1\b Retrieval\b0\par
User asks a question.\par
Similar chunks are retrieved using vector similarity search.\par
Example: top-k relevant chunks.\par
\b Generation\b0\par
Retrieved context + user query are sent to an LLM.\par
LLM generates an accurate, context-aware response.\par
\par

\pard\widctlpar\li360\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qc\ul\b\fs40 LlamaIndex\par

\pard\widctlpar\li360\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\ulnone\b0\fs24 LlamaIndex is an open-source framework designed specifically for connecting LLMs with your private data and building RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) applications.\par
While LangChain connects different components of an AI application, LlamaIndex focuses on organizing, indexing, and retrieving data efficiently.\par
\b Main Purpose\par
\b0 LlamaIndex helps:\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj Load data from documents\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Convert documents into searchable nodes\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Create vector indexes\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Retrieve the most relevant information\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Send retrieved context to an LLM\par

\pard\widctlpar\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\par

\pard\widctlpar\li720\sl300\slmult0\kerning0\b\f1 LlamaIndex Workflow Explanation\par

\pard\widctlpar\li360\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\kerning2\f0 1. Document Loading\par
\b0 The first step is to load data from different sources:\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj PDF files\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Word documents\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Websites\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Databases\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}APIs\par

\pard\widctlpar\li360\sb100\sa100\sl300\slmult0\kerning0\b\f1 2. Node Creation\par

\pard\widctlpar\li720\sb100\sa100\sl300\slmult0\b0\fs21 Large documents are split into smaller pieces called \b nodes\b0 .\par

\pard\widctlpar\li360\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\kerning2\b\f0\fs24 3. Embedding Generation\par
\b0 Each node is converted into a numerical representation called an \b embedding\b0 .\par
\b 4. Vector Index Creation\par
\b0 All node embeddings are stored in a \b Vector Index\b0 .\par
\b 5. Query/Search\par
\b0 A user asks a question: "What are the benefits of AI in healthcare?"\par
The query is also converted into an embedding\par
\b 6. Retrieval\par
\b0 LlamaIndex compares the query embedding with the stored node embeddings.\par
It retrieves the most relevant nodes.\par
This step is called \b semantic retrieval\b0 .\par
\b 7. LLM Processing\par
\b0 The retrieved nodes and user question are sent to the LLM.\par
The LLM now has relevant context to generate an accurate response.\par
\b 8. Final Answer Generation\par
\par

\pard\widctlpar\li360\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qc\fs36 Haystack\par

\pard\widctlpar\li360\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\b0\fs24 Haystack is an open-source framework developed by deepset for building Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), semantic search, question-answering systems, and AI pipelines.\par
It helps developers connect:\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj Documents\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Embedding models\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Vector databases\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Retrievers\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Large Language Models (LLMs)\par

\pard\widctlpar\li360\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj to create intelligent search and chatbot applications.\par
\par
\b\fs28 Haystack Workflow\par
\b0\fs24 1. Document Ingestion\par
Documents are collected from various sources:\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj PDFs\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Word files\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Websites\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Databases\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Knowledge bases\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\b 2. Preprocessing\par
\b0 Before storage, Haystack cleans and splits documents into smaller chunks.\par
\b Tasks Performed\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\b0 Remove unnecessary characters\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Split large documents\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Add metadata\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\b 3. Document Store\par
\b0 The processed chunks are stored in a \b Document Store\b0 .\par
Popular stores:\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj Elasticsearch\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}OpenSearch\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Pinecone\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Weaviate\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}ChromaDB\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb100\sa100\sl300\slmult0\kerning0\b\f1 4. Embedding Generation\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sb100\sa100\sl300\slmult0\b0\fs21 Each document chunk is converted into a vector (embedding).\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb100\sa100\sl300\slmult0\fs24 5. Query Processing\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sb100\sa100\sl300\slmult0 A user enters a question.\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sl300\slmult0\fs21 Haystack converts the question into an embedding.\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sb100\sa100\sl300\slmult0 Now both the documents and the query are represented in the same vector space.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb100\sa100\sl300\slmult0\fs24 6. Retrieval\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sb100\sa100\sl300\slmult0 The Retriever compares the query embedding with stored document embeddings.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb100\sa100\sl300\slmult0\b 7. Prompt Building\par
\b0 Haystack combines:\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sb100\sa100\sl300\slmult0 User Question\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Retrieved Chunks\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb100\sa100\sl300\slmult0 into a structured prompt.\par
\b 8. LLM Generation\par
\b0 The LLM reads the context and generates a response.\par
The model understands the context and formulates an answer.\par
Supported LLMs:\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sb100\sa100\sl300\slmult0 GPT\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Gemini\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Claude\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Llama\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Mistral\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb100\sa100\sl300\slmult0\par
9. Final Answer\par
The answer is grounded in retrieved documents rather than only model memory.\par
\par
